Semiconductor advanced packaging materials play a critical role in protecting integrated circuits, enabling electrical interconnections, managing heat, and maintaining device reliability. These materials are essential to packaging technologies that allow semiconductor manufacturers to integrate more functionality into smaller footprints while improving performance and power efficiency.

The market includes packaging substrates, underfill compounds, die attach materials, epoxy molding compounds, adhesives, and other specialized materials. Their performance influences signal integrity, mechanical stability, thermal dissipation, and the reliability of semiconductor packages under demanding operating conditions.

Demand is increasing as conventional chip-scaling approaches alone become insufficient to meet the performance requirements of AI accelerators, high-performance computing systems, and complex electronic devices. Advanced packaging technologies enable manufacturers to combine multiple dies or chiplets within a single package, increasing the need for materials engineered for precise interconnections and thermal management.

